  "source_review": {
    "input_identity": "Rust, Java and extracted independent Python use public100B PLSTKVAL/seed/id input, nullable versus16B keys, and SHA256(presence || key || value).40 bounded source-semantic input vectors agree; this is not actual cross-language execution.",
    "public_wiring": "Rust uses public Producer::send with no explicit partition; only the uniform profiles choose public StickyPartitioner::seeded. Default RR/null and keyed murmur2 remain distinct. Java imports genuine KafkaProducer/KafkaConsumer and uses partition-null ProducerRecord; adaptive partitioning=false, ignore.keys=false and metrics push=false. Its input seed does not pretend to seed production RNG.",
    "purpose_scope": "All six small profiles explicitly emit qualification/performance_qualified=false and null throughput rates. Warm8192/exercise16384 do not qualify15s/10k warm or60s/1M delivery ranking. Five paired randomized blocks and uncertainty reporting remain separate pending requirements. Public APIs do not observe Java accumulator/RNG history, actual requests/batches/wire bytes, fsync durability, or open-loop/CO-corrected latency.",
    "queues_deadlines": "Rust JoinSet and Java pending/callback ArrayBlockingQueue bound outstanding records at8192. Both use32MiB public producer buffer,10s requests,30s deliveries,5s admission waits and max-in-flight5. Rust join and flush_timeout share absolute90s phase deadline; close_timeout30s follows. Java checks90s between synchronous calls and uses no-timeout flush; host360s producer and910s whole-runtime deadlines own cancellation, so do not claim a Java flush API absolute deadline. Host claims require corrected process inspection.",
    "source_build_contract": "All actual source/build/ELF/classes/jar/config receipts are prerequisites. The manual88-package Cargo.lock has not been resolved. Preserve resolver differences and publish corrected actual lock before immutable offline+locked compile. Debug binaries may establish small correctness cells only; ranking requires release.",
    "verification": "Fresh six-partition zero end-offset baseline precedes production. Rust Consumer assigns every partition at0, checks exact ID/key/value/public ack partition+offset, rejects duplicates and holes, and compares end fences before/after. Offline audit binds two76B-row journals, independent hashes, dense IDs, phase counts, offsets and skew. Actual offline audit and negative data controls remain pending.",
    "warm_exercise_barriers": "Qualification code has zero duration minimum and stops admission exactly at8192 warm plus16384 exercise, with24,576 total cap. Both drain all bounded outstanding calls/callbacks before phase completion. Six source-equivalent scheduler controls cover1/37/8192 completion bursts. No actual records have been sent."
  }
}
